      "fame": 20,
      "intro": "The Paracas Candelabra, also called the Candelabra of the Andes, El Candelabro, Tridente or Tres cruces, is a well-known prehistoric geoglyph found on the northern face of the Paracas Peninsula at Pisco Bay in Peru. Pottery found nearby has been radio carbon dated to 200 BCE, the time of the Paracas culture."
